*** Add File:docs/data_platform_runbook.md
+# Data Platform Runbook (PoC)
+
+This runbook describes quick steps to spin up the data platform PoC components and run a small ingestion -> feature -> query flow.
+
+1. Deploy Kafka (Helm), Zookeeper and ExternalSecrets operator.
+   - helm install kafka bitnami/kafka -f helm/kafka/values.yaml -n data
+
+2. Deploy Debezium connector to capture DB CDC into Kafka.
+   - kubectl apply -f k8s/manifests/debezium-connector-postgres.yaml
+
+3. Deploy Flink jobmanager/worker or use existing Flink cluster and submit ingest jobs via Tekton flink-submit task.
+
+4. Provision S3 data lake and Glue DB via Terraform:
+   - terraform apply -var="..." terraform/aws/data_lake_and_glue.tf
+
+5. Deploy Trino and configure Hive metastore to point at Glue.
+   - helm install trino trino -f helm/trino/values.yaml -n analytics
+
+6. Deploy Feast (offline S3/Parquet store + Redis online store) and run a materialize via feast-materialize-task.
+
+7. Deploy JupyterHub with Keycloak OAuth (values in k8s/manifests/jupyterhub-keycloak-values.yaml).
+   - helm upgrade --install jhub jupyterhub/jupyterhub -f k8s/manifests/jupyterhub-keycloak-values.yaml -n notebook
+
+8. Deploy Amundsen or Amundsen frontend and bootstrap metadata from Glue/Trino.
+
+9. Deploy Superset and connect to Trino catalog for BI dashboards.
+
+10. Add Great Expectations checks into Tekton pipelines as "validation" steps using ops/great_expectations/great_expectations_check.py.
+
+11. For HPC tuning, run services/hpc/rdma_lustre_tuning.sh on compute nodes and run the MPI benchmark manifest services/hpc/mpi_benchmark_job.yaml.
+
+Notes:
+- Use ExternalSecrets to inject Glue/Trino credentials into services.
+- Use vault_stepca_setup.md to provision PKI for device certs (if fleet data ingestion uses device certs).
+- All components must be configured to use Keycloak for SSO in production.
+
